cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ICEtool-gh, please cite it as below, and cite the original ICEtool (see preferred-citation) if your work relies on its underlying model."
title: "ICEtool-gh: a Rhino/Grasshopper port of ICEtool for ground temperature and urban heat island estimation"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Perrault"
    given-names: "Sébastien"
repository-code: "https://github.com/echoesparis/ICEtool-gh"
url: "https://github.com/echoesparis/ICEtool-gh"
license: GPL-3.0
keywords:
  - Rhino
  - Grasshopper
  - urban heat island
  - UHI
  - ground temperature
  - urban planning
  - thermal resilience
abstract: >-
  ICEtool-gh ports ICEtool (a QGIS plugin estimating urban surface/ground
  temperatures for Urban Heat Island analysis, by Arthur Evrard, Egis / INSA
  Toulouse) into Rhino/Grasshopper, running the per-point energy-balance solve
  natively in-canvas through Rhino 8 ScriptEditor-v3 Python components.
